Ordinary images (768 files: 162 GIFs, 300 PNGs, 88 JPEGs and the BMP,
PNM, XPM, XBM files of /usr/share, mkcorpus.sh's 104 files, gen's 27):
identical dumps except a "changed" rectangle of g-wide-small-frames.gif
(the bitmap's width instead of a later frame's re-derived one) and the
pixels an RLE BMP of gen skips (now 0, were uninitialized heap).
The ASan build of the old library reports a heap read before the jump
table for each RLE4/RLE8 BMP mkcorpus.sh writes (ImageMagick ends the
last line with an end of line). The large files decode identically.

Follow-up of a review (4 commits after eaeb44b), new cases; "e95a7cf"
is the library before the branch, "eaeb44b" the branch before these
commits (ASan builds; the result column of the decoder run):

    case                          e95a7cf        eaeb44b        after
    gif-restoreprev-width-0       3 frames       decode fails   3 frames
      (decode)                                   after frame 1
    gif-restoreprev-height-0      3 frames       decode fails   3 frames
      (decode)                                   after frame 1
    gif-restoreprev-canvas        restored area  as e95a7cf     first frame
      (decode)                    and canvas 0                  restored
    gif-wide-small-then-full      third frame    full width     full width
      (decode)                    clipped to
                                  100 columns
    xbm-truncated                 lines 1-3 heap as e95a7cf     0 (white)
                                  (0xbe in ASan)
    jpeg-multiscan-scaled-1g      64x64, 552 MB  as e95a7cf     null
                                  allocation,
                                  829 MB heap

The two "restoreprev" cases with an empty frame failed only at eaeb44b
(QImage::create() of an empty backing store became an error).

Ordinary images after the follow-up against e95a7cf: as above (the
changed rectangle of g-wide-small-frames.gif, the skipped RLE BMP
pixels) and every animation with "restore previous" (disposal 3) whose
backing store grows: the old decoder cleared the whole bitmap there
(anim-prev.gif, anim-bg.gif and anim-opt.gif of mkcorpus.sh, g-anim.gif,
g-anim-trans.gif and g-partly-outside.gif of gen). The three ImageMagick
animations now match "magick FILE -coalesce" in every pixel of every
frame; the old decoder differed in about half of the pixels from the
second frame on. The ASan build reports nothing over the whole corpus.

Intentional behaviour changes of the branch beyond the bounds:

- GIF: on a screen at least 2010 pixels wide or tall, the old decoder
  re-derived the screen from a later small frame (offset plus size) and
  kept that size for the frames after it, so later full-size frames
  were clipped to the small one (gif-wide-small-then-full). The screen
  is now fixed by the first frame: such frames are drawn whole. The
  final images of such animations differ from the old ones.
- JPEG: "GetHeaderInformation" no longer calls jpeg_start_decompress()
  (the size comes from jpeg_calc_output_dimensions()). For a progressive
  file it therefore no longer reads and decodes the whole stream: the
  position of the device after the read differs, and a truncated or
  corrupt progressive file now reports its size instead of failing.
- GIF and XBM pixels that used to be uninitialized heap (a truncated
  XBM) or a wrongly cleared canvas (disposal 3) are now defined; GIFs
  over 256 MiB (8192x8192) are refused (Qt 6's default limit).
